[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known, with one fix queued for the parser. Read report by
report, the merged queue holds three problems with three different fixes. The fix for the parser
closes only the first one.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} repo="xaero6/mega-what-it-shows" issues={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, shift: 3 }} />

<Callout kind="warn">
Keep #4471 open for the parser only. The booking-v3 hint and the one-day shift each have a ticket
of their own, and neither closes when the parser fix ships.
</Callout>

## The three problems

**Parser.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants all write the day first,
so day and month swap whenever both are 12 or less: a reminder for 7 April goes out on 4 July.
These reports come through the app, by email, and through the booking-v2 form.

**booking-v3 hint.** The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People follow
the hint and type the month first, and the form then reads the date day first. The symptom is the
same swap, so subject-line merging put these reports with the parser ones. The fix is in the form,
not in the parser.

**One-day shift.** A handful of reports describe a date that moved by exactly one day: Tuesday
showed as Monday, one meeting landed on Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto. That is not a
swap. It points to a time-zone conversion. The desk already read these as one-day moves
(`desk-notes.json`), but the cause table on #4471 still counts them under the parser.

## Why one ticket hid three

- Merging went by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Different
  causes share the same subjects, so they landed in one ticket.
- Intake tags come from the reporter's browser. The column "intake tag matches" above shows how
  often the tag agrees with the cause: often for the parser, rarely for the hint.
- The export pages overlap, so some reports appear twice. Counts here are by unique report id.

## What the desk can do next

- Before merging into a known ticket, check the cause with [triage](/kb/triage/dedupe), not only the subject.
- When the parser fix ships, re-run this page: reports that keep arriving belong to the other two tickets.

